          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चेतना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चेतना — cetanā — \"consciousness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आहतस्य चेतना शनैः आगच्छति। āhatasya cetanā śanaiḥ āgacchati. The injured man slowly comes round."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चेतना (cetanā) comes from the root √cit, \"to perceive, attend to\"; MW gives cetanā as consciousness and understanding (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
